<title>AUSTRIA: TABLE-Creditanstalt group H1 results.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Creditanstalt group H1 results.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results for the first six months</p>
<p>to June 30, 1997. (Figures in billions of schillings unless</p>
<p>stated).</p>
<p> GROUP						 1997	 1996</p>
<p> Net interest income			    5.337	5.131</p>
<p> Income from securities and investments   1.198	0.852</p>
<p> Net fee and commission income		2.148	1.962</p>
<p> Net profit on trading activities	   1.799	0.900</p>
<p> Operating income				10.855	9.078</p>
<p> Staff expenses				   3.779	3.408</p>
<p> Other administrative expenses		2.463	2.327</p>
<p> Depreciation				     0.306	0.245</p>
<p> Other operating expenses		     0.101	0.057</p>
<p> Operating expenses			     6.649	6.037</p>
<p> Operating result				 4.206	3.041</p>
<p> Net profit					 2.200	1.300</p>
<p>NOTES - Creditanstalt is majority controlled by Bank Austria, which in January acquired two-thirds of the bank's voting shares from the Republic of Austria for 17.2 billion schillings. -- Vienna newsroom, +431 531 12256</p>
